Write feature PRD for {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

LOAD: specification-writing workflows write-feature-prd.md, plan/feature-ba-plan.md.

CHECK COMPLEXITY TIER: shark feature get {{.id}} --json | jq -r '.metadata.complexity_tier' (values: SIMPLE, STANDARD, COMPLEX).

PLAN GATE — run before creating any document:
(1) READ: shark feature context get {{.id}} --json
(2) IF context_data.remaining_steps non-empty: RESUME MODE — skip to ACT with remaining_steps list.
    Log: shark feature note {{.id}} 'Resuming BA. Remaining: [...]. Completed: [...].'
(3) IF context_data.remaining_steps empty: PLAN MODE — run feature-ba-plan.md decision tree.
    FIRST read parent epic docs to understand what is already covered at epic level.
    For each optional doc: state INCLUDE or EXCLUDE with specific reason for THIS feature.
    Default to INCLUDE when uncertain.
    Store: shark feature context set {{.id}} --field remaining_steps '[...]'
           shark feature context set {{.id}} --field implementation_decisions '{...}'
           shark feature context set {{.id}} --field plan_created_at 'TIMESTAMP'
    Log: shark feature note {{.id}} 'PLAN: {tier} tier. Will create N docs. Excluded: [...].' --type=decision

READ:
(1) Parent epic PRD for scope boundaries and requirements traceability (epic must inform feature)
(2) Parent epic context_data to understand what BA docs already cover
(3) Feature description at {{.file_path}}
(4) Triage report or research report for file estimates and integration points
(5) Other feature PRDs in this epic for consistency

ACT: Create only documents in remaining_steps. After each doc, update completed_steps.
     Feature content must be incremental over epic — do not repeat epic-level content.
     Requirements must trace to parent epic requirements.

EXIT GATE:
- All remaining_steps completed
- Tier-appropriate depth: SIMPLE (AC testable), STANDARD (MoSCoW complete, no ambiguity), COMPLEX (all planned files, checklist passes)
- No vague language, no TBDs

